y rather than from the status alone. TRAP: cancelSubscription with cancelImmediately=false writes status \"canceled\" immediately but only sets cancelAt to the period end, so a careful solution that keys the lock on the status (as the trial rule tempts) locks paying customers the moment they schedule a cancellation; the hidden test schedules one at T0, writes at day 13 and expects the lock only from day 14 (and an immediate cancellation to lock at once). Second interaction: the trial-expiry job skips tenants over the free limits, so an ended trial unlocks only when the tenant fits free or picks a plan. Hidden test: 15 cases, all under fake Date pinned to 2026-03-01T09:00Z (lockReasonFor matrix incl. boundary instants; toAppError/isDomainError/402; lock reported on both summaries; issue writes incl. same-status change and board move refused, reads and board intact, no events; comment writes refused, thread intact; project/label/attachment writes refused, reads intact, archived project stays archived; role change/removal/invite/revoke/resend/accept refused with the invitations still pending, no member row, and a revoked token still reported as revoked; settings/flag/webhook writes refused while deleteOrganization succeeds; tenant-scope and permission errors precede the lock, incl. changePlan by an admin; markRead/markAllRead/updatePreference allowed; updateSeats/listInvoices allowed and changePlan unlocks; scheduled cancellation writable through day 13, locked at day 14, immediate cancellation locked at once; trial locked at 14d+1h, expiry job unlocks a tenant that fits free, leaves an over-quota one locked, changePlan unlocks; free plan and no-subscription org never locked; overdue sweep + fan-out, digest, usage rollup and audit record keep working on a locked workspace). Validation: pristine tsc 0 / 617 pass; pristine+hidden exit 1 (the file cannot load: @/lib/billing-lock missing); fresh clone + patch -p1: tsc 0, full suite 632 pass, hidden 3x 15/15 pass; naive A (guards on issue/comment/project/label/attachment only) 2/15 fail; naive B (every guard, but the lock keyed on status so a scheduled cancellation locks at once) 2/15 fail; naive C (every guard, but placed before the permission check in issue/comment services and before the token checks in acceptInvitation) 2/15 fail."
}
